cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "At-Grok Is Not Converged: A Measurement-Validity Audit for Grokking Representation Metrics"
message: "If you use this software or its findings, please cite the paper below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Xuan Khanh"
    family-names: "Truong"
    email: khanh@clevix.vn
    affiliation: "H&K Research Studio / Clevix LLC"
  - given-names: "Duc Trung"
    family-names: "Luu"
    affiliation: "H&K Research Studio / Clevix LLC"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ClevixLab/grokking-compression-clock"
abstract: >-
  A measurement-validity audit for grokking representation metrics. The embedding
  effective rank read at the generalization transition can be a transient that long
  training drives to a low-rank floor, so a snapshot taken at grokking does not
  describe the converged solution. This repository provides the audit, an adversarial
  test suite, processed trajectories, and a one-command pipeline that reproduces every
  table, number, and figure in the paper.
keywords:
  - grokking
  - generalization
  - effective rank
  - measurement validity
  - reproducibility
